preConditionHook:
// Mirrors EasyLanguage's Extremes(), which Highest()/Lowest() call: seeded at
// bar 0 (the window INCLUDES the current bar), scanning bars 1..Length-1 with a
// strict comparison so a tie keeps the earliest bar. Extremes is EL SOURCE, so
// its comparisons carry the ordinary relational tolerance and use el_gt/el_lt.
// The leg is this highest-high / lowest-low window rather than a swing-pivot
// search: SwingHigh/SwingLow are not in the feature register, and the window is
// the standing substitution for a leg.
legHigh = high[0];
legLow = low[0];
for (int i = 1; i < (int)lookback; ++i) {
    if (el_gt(high[i], legHigh)) legHigh = high[i];
    if (el_lt(low[i], legLow)) legLow = low[i];
}
// pullbackLookback MEASURES THE PULLBACK OVER A WINDOW RATHER THAN AT THIS BAR
// (added in the final review in place of a separate DeepPullbackMeansRange
// rule): the depth is taken from the lowest low of the last pullbackLookback
// bars (long) / the highest high of them (short), so a pullback that reached
// the threshold a few bars ago still counts. At the default 1 the window is the
// current bar alone -- the window collapses to low[0] / high[0] -- and the rule
// is unchanged, so no existing placement moves. Same Extremes() seeding as the
// leg loop above.
pbHigh = high[0];
pbLow = low[0];
for (int i = 1; i < (int)pullbackLookback; ++i) {
    if (el_gt(high[i], pbHigh)) pbHigh = high[i];
    if (el_lt(low[i], pbLow)) pbLow = low[i];
}

//
// AMENDED 2026-09-22 (Grimes A list, RetracementDepthWithinBand): the new
// maxRetracementFraction input turns the floor into a BAND, so the pullback must
// have retraced between retracementFraction and maxRetracementFraction of the
// leg behind it. Grimes expects pullback terminations around 50 percent and
// anywhere in the 25 to 75 percent range (G03-20), so an unusually SHALLOW
// pullback and an unusually DEEP one both fail; his 0.25 / 0.75 edges live in
// the catalog row and the grid, NOT in the defaults.
//
// A BAND IS NOT THIS RULE NEGATED -- a pullback that never got near the leg
// fails the band and passes the negation -- exactly the
// PullbackNearMissesEntryPrice / ShallowDipBelowPriorBarLow precedent and merge
// decision 19.
//
// maxRetracementFraction DEFAULTS TO 1000, large enough to be inert: with
// pullbackLookback <= lookback the pullback's extreme lies inside the leg
// window, so the depth can never exceed the leg's own height and the upper bound
// can never bite. Every existing placement and template is unchanged.
//
// Written as a MULTIPLICATION on both bounds, so a zero-height leg still cannot
// divide by zero -- and at a zero-height leg the depth is 0 and both bounds
// hold.
